# Manual REST Client requests for GET and POST /locations (VS Code REST Client).
# Sign in with an approved review account of REVIEW_ACCOUNTS in apps/backend/.env: set the email and code below.
# Codes are read from the backend log when RESEND_API_KEY is unset.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@email = admin@example.com
@code = 345678

### Request a sign-in code (expects 202)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/code
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "locale": "pt-BR"
}

### Sign in (expects 200 with accessToken)
# @name session
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}

###
@token = {{session.response.body.accessToken}}

### List every location, sorted by name ignoring case and accents (expects 200 with { items: [{ id, name, address }] }; any approved account)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a location (expects 201 with { id, name, address }; admins only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Praia do Futuro",
  "address": "Av. Zezé Diogo, 5000 – Fortaleza"
}

### The same name ignoring case and accents (expects 409 location.name.duplicate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "práia do futuro",
  "address": "Outro endereço"
}

### Empty name and address (expects 422 with errors location.name.required and location.address.required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "address": ""
}

### Without a token (expects 401 auth.token.invalid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locations

### As a student or instructor (expects 403 user.role.notAdmin on POST): use that account's token
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Outro local",
  "address": "Rua A"
}
